// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_powershell_enable_susp_windows_optional_feature.yml
// ID Sigma: c740d4cf-a1e9-41de-bb16-8a46a4f57918
// Título: Potential Suspicious Windows Feature Enabled - ProcCreation
// Descripción: Detects usage of the built-in PowerShell cmdlet "Enable-WindowsOptionalFeature" used as a Deployment Image Servicing and Management tool.
Similar to DISM.exe, this cmdlet is used to enumerate, install, uninstall, configure, and update features and packages in Windows images

// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: medium
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_powershell_enable_susp_windows_optional_feature.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "Enable-WindowsOptionalFeature" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-Online" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-FeatureName") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "TelnetServer" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Internet-Explorer-Optional-amd64" or ProcessCommandLine contains "TFTP" or ProcessCommandLine contains "SMB1Protocol" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Client-ProjFS" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Microsoft-Windows-Subsystem-Linux")
